1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Your map is a grid. The world is not.

2
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:03,200
sin and cos are the translation.

3
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:06,400
You, here. The place you want, there.

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,800
Your phone says: 5 km, that way.

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,200
But a map only speaks east and north.

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:14,400
Two languages for the same place.

7
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:17,600
That direction, in numbers: cos θ = 0.8, sin θ = 0.6.

8
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:20,000
Now the distance. It is r, and it is 5.

9
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,400
Both rows. One journey, two answers.

10
00:00:22,400 --> 00:00:25,200
5 × 0.8 = 4. Four kilometres east.

11
00:00:25,200 --> 00:00:28,000
5 × 0.6 = 3. Three kilometres north.

12
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,400
Go 4 east, then 3 north. Same place — but that walk is 7 km.

13
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,800
Every sat-nav, every delivery app, every game character.

14
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:34,000
We learned this at school.

15
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,200
Nobody ever said what for.

16
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:36,800
Send this to your school friend — and tell them THIS is how it's solved.

17
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:40,000
Follow for the math behind AI. @observer.collapse
